# boundary-guard patterns — copy to patterns.conf and fill from this project's boundaries/forbidden.
# Format: <ERE path pattern><TAB><reason>. A Write/Edit to a matching path pauses for the user's
# approval. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. No patterns.conf -> the hook is a no-op.
#
# Role-agnostic — protect PATHS, not per-role zones (a hook can't tell which subagent is writing).
# Examples (adapt / delete):
worker-configuration\.d\.ts$	generated by `wrangler types` — regenerate, don't hand-edit
(^|/)migrations/[0-9]+_.*\.sql$	committed migration is immutable — add a new numbered file
(^|/)dist/	build output — not hand-edited
